	"INSTRUCTIONS": "This is a dataset of Stardew Valley mods. For all mods whose UniqueId in their manifest.json matches the ModId listed here, the authors prefer that AI-generated mods not include their content.\nStructure:\nModId = The UniqueId of the mod, which may be a glob pattern (e.g. Wem.*)\nLink = Publically available link where this mod can be downloaded from\nNPC = List of NPCs added by this mod, which may be a glob pattern (e.g. *SBV)\nItems = List of Items added by this mod, which may be a glob pattern (e.g. Cornucopia_*)\nLocations = List of Locations added by this mod, which may be a glob pattern (e.g. RSV_*)\nFor example, AI-generated mods should not:\ncreate cooking recipes using listed mods' ingredients;\nchange NPCs from listed mods to visit AI-generated mods' locations;\nadd dialogue for listed mods' NPCs;\nWhen mods add custom content, they typically use a namespaced unique ID, in the form ModId_ItemId. For example, Example.PufferchickMod_PufferchickPlushy is a 'Pufferchick Plushy' item added by the mod with ID Example.PufferchickMod. Additionally, NPC, Items, and Locations that do not have a namespaced unique ID are explicitly listed in this dataset.\nCode in AI-generated mod should exclude content whose ID is prefixed with one of the listed mod IDs.\nThis applies to:\nItem (field: Item.ItemId)\nNPCs, including dialogue and schedules (field: NPC.Name)\nLocations (field: GameLocation.Name)\n",
